.TH ZTOP 1 "2026-11-15" "ztop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ztop \- a system monitor for one host and your fleet, in a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ztop
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ztop
shows processes with CPU, memory and I/O meters in a terminal, and can
watch a whole fleet of hosts. On Linux and macOS it samples the local
host; the
.BR capture ,
.BR agent ,
.B hub
and
.B connect
subcommands record raw inputs, serve them over the loopback interface,
and drive the TUI from a remote host.
.SS Options
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pids " " \fIPIDS\fP
Show only these process ids, comma separated.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delay " " \fISECONDS\fP
Seconds between samples; fractional values are allowed, and anything
below 0.1 is refused so the loop cannot spin.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user " " \fIUSER\fP
Show only this user's processes at startup.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-sort " " \fIKEY\fP
Sort by this key at startup: one of
.BR pid ", " user ", " cpu ", " mem ", " res ", " virt ", " shr ", "
.BR pri ", " nice ", " time ", " start ", " core ", " ppid ", " name ", "
.BR command .
Unknown keys are refused.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tree
Start in tree view.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Render without colors, ignoring the saved theme for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-readonly
Refuse every action that changes the system: signals and renice are
disabled for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print help. \fB\-\-version\fP prints the version.
.SS Keys
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc ", " Ctrl\-C
quit
.TP
.B F1
help; any key closes it
.TP
.B Z
pause/resume updates
.TP
.B Ctrl\-L
redraw the screen
.TP
.B F2
setup (theme, tree view, meter style, the I/O, pressure and sensors lines, the
header meter layout; saved)
.TP
.B F3
search (Esc/Enter close, F3 repeats)
.TP
.B F4
filter by name
.TP
.B u
filter by user
.TP
.B Tab
cycle the sort column
.TP
.B i
flip the sort direction
.TP
.BR M ", " P ", " T
sort by memory, cpu, time
.TP
.B f
follow a process
.TP
.B F5
tree view; Enter collapses a node
.TP
.BR j ", " k
move the cursor
.TP
.BR Space ", " c ", " U
tag row, tag children, untag all
.TP
.BR F9 ", " K
send a signal to the tagged rows
.TP
.BR F7 ", " F8
renice \-1 / +1
.TP
.BR I ", " A
set the I/O priority (best\-effort/realtime/idle classes and levels) or
the CPU affinity (all cores, or one core) of the tagged rows; Linux
only \- on macOS applying reports that the action is unavailable
.TP
.BR H
cycle thread visibility: show userland threads, then hide kernel
threads, then back (Linux reports thread rows; kernel threads are shown
and userland threads hidden by default)
.TP
.BR p
toggle the program path in the name column (the path shows whenever the
system reports one)
.TP
.BR e ", " l
read the environment or the open files of the tagged rows (else the
cursor's row) live from the OS into a popup: j/k scroll, Esc or q closes;
what the OS allows decides the outcome \- a same\-user process works
unprivileged, another user's process needs privileges, and the OS error
shows in the status line
.TP
.BR s
trace the tagged rows' (else the cursor's row) syscalls into a popup: one
line per completed syscall with its name and return value, the tail
followed as it arrives, j/k scrolls back, Esc or q stops the tracer and
closes; Linux only (ptrace), and only where the OS allows the attach \-
a child of ztop always works, another user's process needs privileges,
and macOS reports unavailable
.TP
.BR a ", " d ", " n ", " o ", " t
silicon, disks, network, io, thermal
.PP
The screens are also tabs: every screen except the process table shows a
tab strip above its panel with the active screen bracketed, and a click
on a label switches screens.
.PP
The mouse works too: a click selects a row, a click on a column header
sorts by it, and a click on the function bar replays that key.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/Library/Application Support/ztop/config.json
(macOS) or
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ztop/config.json
(Linux): the saved setup, theme, tree view, line toggles and meter layout.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ztop
Monitor the local host.
.TP
.B ztop \-d 0.5 \-s cpu \-u alice
Refresh twice a second, sorted by CPU, showing one user.
.TP
.B ztop \-\-readonly
Monitor without being able to signal or renice anything.
.TP
.B ztop capture \-\-out capture
Record this host's raw inputs as a fixture for collector tests.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR top (1),
.BR htop (1),
.BR kill (1),
.BR renice (1)
